From 78185ebc13a17fb2e1ff24cea6c7774f5fb9812b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 06:17:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] perf(control-plane): stop purging dedup keys on every
 lookup

ProcessedKeyStore ran a DELETE of expired keys followed by a commit on
every seen and mark call, so each reconcile turned a read into a write
transaction on the shared database file.

seen now ignores keys whose created_at is older than the TTL, so its
result no longer depends on when expired rows are removed. The DELETE
runs at most once per min(ttl, 60s); the first call after start-up
still removes keys left behind by a previous run.
---
 .../controlplane/reconciler/dedup.py          | 45 ++++++++++++-------
 tests/unit/controlplane/test_dedup_store.py   | 37 ++++++++++++++-
 2 files changed, 66 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

